# Frontend Architecture

- Use Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and CSS variables for design tokens.
- Prefer Server Components. Add `use client` only for browser state or interaction.
- Routes fetch and compose data; sections assemble page content; UI components remain CMS-agnostic.
- Map CMS documents to typed view models at the data boundary.
- Validate external data before rendering and provide loading, empty, error, and unavailable states.
- Keep component APIs small. Prefer explicit variants over multiple boolean flags.
- Use stable aspect ratios and responsive constraints to prevent layout shift.
- Use `next/image`; define meaningful sizes, alt behavior, and mobile art direction.
- Use Framer Motion for necessary component motion. Reserve GSAP for approved complex timelines.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; avoid autoplay carousels and autoplay video with sound.
- Keep mobile behavior equal in importance to desktop; never require hover to reveal essential content.
- Use semantic HTML, visible focus, keyboard support, and WCAG 2.2 AA contrast.
